Adreno650 01db67e0: NativeAdrenoVm::map(nullptr, ...) returns kIOReturnBadArgument instead of dereferencing null

Since 1c4065c (perf(vm): map owned and exclusive imported memory without alias scans) map() calls
exclusivePages(memory, cls) before preflight(), and exclusivePages dereferences memory first: a null object
crashes the kernel instead of being refused. The fork's test_vm calls map(nullptr, ...) and expects
kIOReturnBadArgument (found by running it in a host build once its SMMU peer accepts TLBIVAL, see 0002).
Upstream Adreno740 (122a8f1) has the same guard; this backports exactly that line.

